# `.env` holds SCHEDULE_DB_PASSWORD and SCHEDULE_TOKEN.  A file in the build
# context is a file in the daemon's cache and in every layer that copies it, and
# `docker push` ships the layers — deleting the file in a later RUN does not help.
# The image also never reads one (see config.py: the .env fallback resolves to a
# path inside site-packages that does not exist), so there is nothing to lose.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Everything below is not needed to build the wheel, and keeping it out of the
# context is what makes the COPY in the Dockerfile safe by construction.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/
.kilo/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.venv*/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
tests/
scripts/
*.crt
*.pem
*.key
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
opencode.json

# `*.md` is excluded wholesale, then README.md is put back: pyproject declares
# `readme = "README.md"`, so the metadata build fails without it.
*.md
!README.md
